      "side": 1,
      "message": "Please fix this WARNING reported by autoreview issue finding: By returning the stamp file solely as an implicit dependency, you are effectively promoting all `order_only` dependencies contained within the stamp to `implicit` dependencies for the caller. \n\nIn Ninja, if `target` depends on `stamp` via `|`, and `stamp` depends on `hard_dep` via `||`, then whenever `hard_dep` changes, `stamp` is rebuilt, and consequently `target` is rebuilt because it\u0027s an implicit dependency of `stamp`.\n\nThis will cause unintended rebuilds, especially for C++ targets where hard dependencies (like generated headers) are supposed to be order-only to avoid recompiling every file when a header changes.\n\nTo fix this, you might need to return two separate stamp files (one for implicit and one for order-only) or find a way to let the caller handle the two sets of dependencies even when grouped.",
